  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the line $y=4x-1$ passes through the points $Q(0,-1)$ and $R(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $Q$ and $R$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${Q}^{\u2032}(3,-2)$ and ${R}^{\u2032}(-10,6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${Q}^{\u2032}$ and ${R}^{\u2032}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{-10-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{8}{13}(x-3) \\\\ 13y+26 & =-8x+24 \\\\ 8x+13y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
